'' TWO MODULES' HEADERS SHARE ONE HEADER: hg/w's interface carries shared.bi, and hg/pub's PUBLIC
'' header includes it too. Imported w first, the importer holds shared.bi's guard -- from
'' shared.bi -- when hg/pub's '#tki undef shared_bi_guard' asks; the module read it undefined
'' and shared.bi then defined it, so that is the same header read once, not TKO0370 (the shape
'' of sys/win then vendor/SDL3, whose crt guards were refused).
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 --no-module-cache -i tests/modules/src/hdrguard/libs tests/modules/src/hdrguard/app/wfirst.tiko -o tests/modules/hdrguardw.exe
'' ENV: TIKO_LIBPATH=build/obj/rtlib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-NOT: TKO0370
'' RUN: tests/modules/hdrguardw.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  7              5
